Ola Maps | Ola Maps API Reference > POST /routing/v1/routeOptimizer

POST /routing/v1/routeOptimizer
Route Optimizer API
Computes the most efficient route by reordering a list of waypoints to minimize overall travel time, based on estimated time of arrival (ETA).  This API supports round trips, fixed or flexible start/end points, and congestion-aware routing when enabled.

Parameters:

- x-request-id (header, optional): Unique ID for tracing the request. {"type": "string"}

- x-correlation-id (header, optional): Correlation ID for distributed tracing across systems. {"type": "string"}

- locations (query, required): Pipe-separated list of coordinates in `lat,lng` format. Maximum of **25 points**.

 {"type": "string"}

- source (query, optional): Source waypoint. Allowed values: `first`, `any`.

 {"type": "string", "default": "first"}

- destination (query, optional): Destination waypoint. Allowed values: `last`, `any`.

 {"type": "string", "default": "last"}

- round_trip (query, optional): Whether the optimized route should return to the starting point. _Note: If `round_trip = false`, source=any and destination=any is not supported._

 {"type": "boolean", "default": false}

- mode (query, optional): Travel mode - `driving`, `walking`, `bike`, or `auto`. {"type": "string", "default": "driving"}

- steps (query, optional): Whether step-by-step instructions are included. {"type": "boolean", "default": true}

- overview (query, optional): Level of overview geometry - `full`, `simplified`, or `false`. {"type": "string", "default": "full"}

